config BK7258_BT_IPC
	bool "N12 official Beken Bluetooth mailbox IPC wrapper"
	default n
	depends on BK7258_RPTUN_MBOX
	depends on !BK7258_AP_CORE || (DRIVERS_BLUETOOTH && NET_BLUETOOTH && WIRELESS_BLUETOOTH)
	---help---
		Use the official SDK MB_CHNL_BT_CMD protocol without modifying either
		NuttX or the SDK.  The CP image starts the Beken controller-side IPC
		worker.  The AP image registers a board-owned bt_driver_s lower half,
		translates NuttX HCI command/ACL packets to bt_ipc_* calls and copies
		SDK event/ACL callbacks into the stock NuttX Bluetooth Host.

		This is independent of the generic RPTUN/RPMsg services: both share the
		SDK physical mailbox dispatcher but reserve different logical channels.
		The initial profile supports HCI command, event and ACL traffic; SCO and
		ISO are deliberately out of scope.

