config BK7258_BT_IPC_TRACE
	bool "N13 Bluetooth host stack boundary counters"
	default n
	depends on BK7258_BT_IPC_TEST && BK7258_AP_CORE
	---help---
		Wrap the stock NuttX Bluetooth host boundary functions and expose
		monotonic counters through the existing bkbttest stats operation.
		Except for separately selected compatibility fixes, the wrappers call
		the original implementation unchanged.  They are a board-owned
		diagnostic aid for the HCI, L2CAP/ATT and connection-TX path and do not
		modify NuttX or the Beken SDK.

config BK7258_BT_CONN_RX_REF_COMPAT
	bool "N13 inbound ACL connection-reference compatibility wrapper"
	default n
	depends on BK7258_BT_IPC_TRACE
	---help---
		Release the caller-owned bt_conn reference after the stock
		bt_conn_receive implementation returns.  The current NuttX hci_acl
		path obtains one reference with bt_conn_lookup_handle for every inbound
		ACL packet but does not release it, so a completed GATT session leaves
		the single connection slot permanently occupied.

		This board-owned link wrapper keeps NuttX unmodified.  The N13 verifier
		checks the exact upstream ownership pattern and fails closed if the
		NuttX implementation changes, preventing a future double release.

config BK7258_BT_ATT_MTU_COMPAT
	bool "N13 oversized peer ATT MTU compatibility wrapper"
	default n
	depends on BK7258_BT_IPC_TRACE
	---help---
		Clamp an inbound ATT Exchange MTU request above the stock NuttX host
		limit to that limit before passing it to the unmodified host stack.
		This preserves the normal server-side minimum negotiation while working
		around the stock host rejecting newer peers that advertise a larger
		receive capability.  The wrapper is board-owned and exposes a hit count
		through bkbttest stats.

