config BK7258_PSRAM
	bool "N14 official-driver PSRAM wrapper and role-local heaps"
	default n
	depends on ARCH_CHIP_BK7258
	---help---
		Initialize PSRAM only from CP through the official Beken bk_psram_init
		API, then expose disjoint board-owned NuttX MM heaps to the SDK
		psram_* ABI.  The heap ranges exactly preserve the v3.1.1.9 default
		8 MiB ram_regions.csv contract: CP 0x60700000+0x20000 and AP
		0x60720000+0xa0000.  Matching the official v3.1.1.9 MPU table,
		region 6 maps the 0x60000000..0x63ffffff PSRAM aperture as
		Non-shareable Normal Non-cacheable on CP plus both AP logical CPUs.
		PSRAM remains powered for the complete N14 boot generation;
		sleep/power-down ownership is out of scope.

config BK7258_PSRAM_MEDIA
	bool
	default n
	depends on BK7258_PSRAM && BK7258_AP_CORE
	help
		Enable the AP-side wrapper for the official v3.1.1.9 PSRAM media
		slabs.  Large media buffers use the SDK-defined USER, AUDIO,
		ENCODE and YUV regions instead of exhausting the 640 KiB AP
		general-purpose PSRAM heap.

config BK7258_PSRAM_BOOT_TEST
	bool "N14 destructive full-capacity PSRAM boot test"
	default n
	depends on BK7258_PSRAM && !BK7258_AP_CORE
	---help---
		After the official CP driver detects the device and before either
		role-local heap or AP starts, run walking-data, address-alias,
		address-derived, inverse and final-zero passes over the complete
		detected 8 MiB or 16 MiB device.  This is safe only at that boot
		boundary and deliberately has no runtime command that could overwrite
		live heaps or future media slabs.  Enable in the N14 validation
		profile, not in a latency-sensitive production profile.

